module Proof
  # Raised when a project file can't be read, with the file, the line, and what
  # is wrong.
  #
  # A project file is text that a person writes, and Proof reads it before it
  # sends anything. A mistake in it that Proof ignored would run a task with
  # settings the person didn't mean. A message that names no line leaves them
  # searching the file.
  #
  # This error is the one every mistake in a project file raises, whether KDL
  # refuses the text or Proof refuses what it says. It is a
  # `Proof::FileError`, so its message is the path, the line, and the reason.
  #
  # Use it to show a person where the file went wrong, or to answer a refusal
  # with exit status 2.
  #
  # ## Examples
  #
  # ```ruby
  # error = Proof::ProjectFileError.new(path: ".config/proof.kdl", line: 7, reason: "a label has no space")
  # error.message # => ".config/proof.kdl:7: a label has no space"
  # error.line # => 7
  # ```
  #
  # A mistake with no line leaves the line out of the message:
  #
  # ```ruby
  # error = Proof::ProjectFileError.new(path: ".config/proof.kdl", line: nil, reason: "this is a symbolic link")
  # error.message # => ".config/proof.kdl: this is a symbolic link"
  # ```
  class ProjectFileError < FileError
  end
end
